<article class="app-prose app-prose--summary">
    <h2>Capture and revisit questions</h2>
    <p>
        Curiosity Tracker helps you capture the questions, ideas, links and topics you want to come back to. Save curiosities the moment they come to you, organise them with tags and statuses, and attach the webpages and PDFs that go with them. When the time is right, Curiosity Tracker resurfaces them, so good ideas don’t disappear into notes, open tabs or memory.
    </p>
    <p>
        Curiosity Tracker is for iPhone and iPad, and it is free.
    </p>

    <h3>Capture</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Add a question or idea in seconds.</li>
        <li>Share webpages, text and PDFs straight from Safari, Files and other apps.</li>
        <li>Add curiosities hands-free with Siri and Shortcuts.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Organise</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Sort curiosities by status: Open, Exploring or Answered.</li>
        <li>Tag them yourself, or let the app suggest tags from what you’ve written.</li>
        <li>Search across prompts, notes and tags.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Revisit</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Resurfacing brings older curiosities back when they’re ready for another look.</li>
        <li>Push an idea back to next week when now isn’t the right time.</li>
        <li>See patterns in what you explore with Insights.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Stay on track</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Set a daily or weekly research goal.</li>
        <li>Follow your progress on the Lock Screen and in the Dynamic Island with a Live Activity.</li>
        <li>Get optional reminders so you don’t lose momentum.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Sync and privacy</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Your curiosities, links and PDFs sync across your devices through your own private iCloud.</li>
        <li>No accounts, ads, tracking or third-party analytics.</li>
        <li>Your content is stored on your device and in your iCloud, never on our servers.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Curiosity Tracker is a quiet personal thinking tool, not a social network, a feed or a heavy productivity system. It gives your questions a home and brings them back when you’re ready to explore them. The <a href="/apps/curiosity-tracker/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains how your information is handled.
    </p>
</article>
